1
00:00:27,048 --> 00:00:31,678
[birds twittering]

2
00:00:49,738 --> 00:00:51,740
[approaching footsteps]

3
00:01:18,016 --> 00:01:19,684
[squealing]

4
00:01:36,451 --> 00:01:39,079
- [squealing]
- [grunting]

5
00:01:46,419 --> 00:01:48,880
[yelling, grunting]

6
00:02:19,744 --> 00:02:22,747
- [man shouts]
- [animal howls]

7
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,803
[shrieks]

8
00:02:43,435 --> 00:02:45,854
[panting]

9
00:02:53,194 --> 00:02:56,072
[all chuckling]

10
00:03:21,139 --> 00:03:23,099
The heart...

11
00:03:31,066 --> 00:03:32,567
...for Smoke Frog.

12
00:03:32,567 --> 00:03:33,818
Thank you.

13
00:03:39,991 --> 00:03:42,369
This liver for Curl Nose.

14
00:03:42,369 --> 00:03:44,120
[Curl Nose] Thank you.

15
00:03:48,917 --> 00:03:50,335
Cocoa Leaf...

16
00:03:50,335 --> 00:03:51,670
...the ears.

17
00:03:51,670 --> 00:03:52,963
Thank you.

18
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,384
And for you Blunted...

19
00:04:00,178 --> 00:04:01,805
...the balls.

20
00:04:04,432 --> 00:04:06,267
Not this again.

21
00:04:06,267 --> 00:04:07,686
I'm helping you.

22
00:04:07,686 --> 00:04:09,479
Then you eat them!

23
00:04:09,479 --> 00:04:11,606
I don't need them. Neither do
the rest of the fellows.

24
00:04:11,606 --> 00:04:12,691
Do you fellows?

25
00:04:12,691 --> 00:04:13,525
[all] No.

26
00:04:13,525 --> 00:04:14,567
Of course not!

27
00:04:14,567 --> 00:04:16,069
Sometimes!

28
00:04:16,069 --> 00:04:17,237
What do you think?

29
00:04:17,237 --> 00:04:18,113
No!

30
00:04:18,113 --> 00:04:19,614
No, no!

31
00:04:19,614 --> 00:04:21,616
But how many times does it take?

32
00:04:21,616 --> 00:04:24,577
I have eight older sisters
and one brother.

33
00:04:24,577 --> 00:04:27,998
Father took tapir balls
all ten times.

34
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:09,914
Shall I tell him?

35
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:14,252
I'm sorry.
The balls are useless.

36
00:05:16,504 --> 00:05:18,006
You've never had them?

37
00:05:18,006 --> 00:05:20,467
Couldn't tell you
what they taste like.

38
00:05:21,468 --> 00:05:22,594
None of you?

39
00:05:24,596 --> 00:05:27,265
No, but it's been fun
watching you...

40
00:05:33,104 --> 00:05:34,105
This was your idea!

41
00:05:37,108 --> 00:05:38,651
Get him off me!

42
00:05:38,651 --> 00:05:40,987
- [grunting]
- [all shouting]

43
00:05:45,283 --> 00:05:46,910
Calm down!

44
00:06:04,344 --> 00:06:07,847
Why do you let them
treat you like this?

45
00:06:07,847 --> 00:06:10,016
Be strong.

46
00:06:10,016 --> 00:06:11,434
Where is your pride?

47
00:06:16,481 --> 00:06:19,526
It all works...Yes?

48
00:06:22,987 --> 00:06:24,697
Yes...

49
00:06:24,697 --> 00:06:27,492
...I just can't make children.

50
00:06:32,914 --> 00:06:36,167
There is something
I will tell you...

51
00:06:36,167 --> 00:06:39,462
...but I warn you,
it's very powerful.

52
00:06:41,089 --> 00:06:41,881
What do you speak of?

53
00:06:42,674 --> 00:06:44,300
The soanzo leaf.

54
00:06:45,677 --> 00:06:47,345
The soanzo leaf?

55
00:06:47,345 --> 00:06:50,014
From the great marshes
in the south...

56
00:06:54,853 --> 00:06:57,856
This is what gave me
my ten children.

57
00:07:04,195 --> 00:07:06,406
No! No! Wait...

58
00:07:07,740 --> 00:07:10,785
You have to rub
them on...down there.

59
00:07:10,785 --> 00:07:13,288
Just before you next try.

60
00:07:13,288 --> 00:07:15,373
Apply it generously...

61
00:07:19,961 --> 00:07:22,046
I don't know how to thank you.

62
00:07:24,048 --> 00:07:27,635
If this works...
maybe she'll stop bothering me.

63
00:07:27,635 --> 00:07:29,220
Your wife?

64
00:07:29,220 --> 00:07:31,389
No, her mother.

65
00:07:31,389 --> 00:07:33,766
The old hag wants grandchildren.

66
00:07:43,318 --> 00:07:45,403
Give me some meat.

67
00:07:45,403 --> 00:07:47,780
Here, work on this...

68
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:49,616
...pure meat...

69
00:07:51,284 --> 00:07:53,620
...ball breath.

70
00:07:55,997 --> 00:07:58,416
- [grunts]
- [all laugh]

71
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:10,637
[rumbling]

72
00:08:58,059 --> 00:08:59,185
What do you want?

73
00:09:03,648 --> 00:09:04,941
What do you want?

74
00:09:09,028 --> 00:09:11,114
[leaves rustling]

75
00:10:00,413 --> 00:10:02,206
I am Flint Sky.

76
00:10:02,206 --> 00:10:05,585
I have hunted this forest
from the day I came of age.

77
00:10:07,086 --> 00:10:11,507
My father hunted this forest
with me and before me.

78
00:10:13,134 --> 00:10:15,386
Jaguar Paw, my son.

79
00:10:15,386 --> 00:10:17,722
He hunts this forest with me.

80
00:10:19,265 --> 00:10:22,727
He will hunt it with his son
after I am gone.

81
00:10:42,914 --> 00:10:44,248
A good catch?

82
00:10:45,083 --> 00:10:47,085
Good waters here.

83
00:10:49,754 --> 00:10:51,214
The forest gives much here.

84
00:10:57,303 --> 00:10:59,263
We ask only to pass through.

85
00:11:00,098 --> 00:11:01,432
Pass.

86
00:11:07,271 --> 00:11:09,107
Keep safe as you pass.

87
00:11:12,777 --> 00:11:14,320
Let's go.

88
00:11:20,493 --> 00:11:23,788
- [baby cries]
- [indistinct whispering]

89
00:11:51,149 --> 00:11:53,276
Our lands were ravaged.

90
00:11:54,152 --> 00:11:56,112
We seek a new beginning.

91
00:12:03,077 --> 00:12:04,662
Your lands were ravaged?

92
00:12:08,374 --> 00:12:10,001
Yes...

93
00:12:11,335 --> 00:12:14,589
We seek a new beginning...

94
00:12:14,589 --> 00:12:16,090
Be still.

95
00:12:16,090 --> 00:12:17,008
My son!

96
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:20,303
Be still.

97
00:12:25,433 --> 00:12:26,726
Back to the village.

98
00:12:37,695 --> 00:12:40,323
[howling]

99
00:12:50,458 --> 00:12:53,127
[chirping]

100
00:13:00,468 --> 00:13:05,389
I ask you not to speak of what
you saw in the forest today.

101
00:13:09,268 --> 00:13:11,646
You are troubled.

102
00:13:11,646 --> 00:13:13,397
Yes, I am.

103
00:13:21,322 --> 00:13:24,492
[indistinct chatter]

104
00:13:29,914 --> 00:13:34,585
Those people in the forest,
what did you see on them?

105
00:13:34,585 --> 00:13:35,753
I do not understand.

106
00:13:36,837 --> 00:13:38,297
Fear.

107
00:13:41,592 --> 00:13:45,137
Deep rotting fear.

108
00:13:45,137 --> 00:13:47,723
They were infected by it.

109
00:13:48,599 --> 00:13:50,434
Did you see?

110
00:13:50,434 --> 00:13:52,603
Fear is a sickness.

111
00:13:57,858 --> 00:14:01,988
It will crawl into the soul
of anyone who engages it.

112
00:14:03,781 --> 00:14:07,952
It has tainted
your peace already.

113
00:14:10,162 --> 00:14:14,292
I did not raise you
to see you live with fear.

114
00:14:16,794 --> 00:14:18,713
Strike it from your heart.

115
00:14:18,713 --> 00:14:21,966
Do not bring it
into our village.

116
00:14:21,966 --> 00:14:25,636
At first light we
will gather with the elders...

117
00:14:25,636 --> 00:14:30,391
...at the sacred hill
of our fathers.

118
00:14:30,391 --> 00:14:35,313
There we will call on
their spirits to guide us.

119
00:14:35,313 --> 00:14:37,440
[children laughing]

120
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:45,823
[growling]

121
00:14:45,823 --> 00:14:47,533
Oh, here he is!

122
00:14:48,492 --> 00:14:49,827
The big lump!

123
00:14:50,661 --> 00:14:52,121
He's useless.

124
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:54,415
He can't do it.

125
00:14:54,415 --> 00:14:56,167
[all laughing]

126
00:14:56,167 --> 00:14:58,377
You! Yes you!

127
00:14:58,377 --> 00:15:01,797
With your height and your girth.
You have deceived us.

128
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:04,133
Get inside!

129
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,515
Damn you! Get in there!

130
00:15:11,515 --> 00:15:13,434
Old woman, please.

131
00:15:13,434 --> 00:15:14,393
Move it!

132
00:15:18,773 --> 00:15:20,232
You don't work!

133
00:15:22,777 --> 00:15:24,236
What are you laughing about?

134
00:15:32,203 --> 00:15:36,707
Give me a grandchild
or I will have you replaced.

135
00:15:37,875 --> 00:15:40,586
Mother, that's enough.

136
00:15:40,586 --> 00:15:43,881
Do not come out
until you make a child.

137
00:15:45,549 --> 00:15:47,301
Two would be better!

138
00:15:47,301 --> 00:15:48,219
What?

139
00:15:49,887 --> 00:15:51,889
Twins you oaf.

140
00:16:00,606 --> 00:16:02,483
Mother.

141
00:16:02,483 --> 00:16:07,154
Can you go away? He says he
can't with you sitting there.

142
00:16:07,154 --> 00:16:08,531
Just get busy.

143
00:16:09,782 --> 00:16:11,075
Mom...

144
00:16:15,746 --> 00:16:17,206
She's gone.

145
00:16:18,082 --> 00:16:19,834
[shouting]

146
00:17:00,791 --> 00:17:03,794
Mother, what do you say we should have
at the feast tonight?

147
00:17:03,794 --> 00:17:07,089
I have tapir...
but I also found this boy.

148
00:17:07,089 --> 00:17:08,090
[Mother] I say boy.

149
00:17:08,090 --> 00:17:09,592
Roasted!

150
00:17:09,592 --> 00:17:12,303
The tapir smells better.
I think it's more fresh.

151
00:17:12,303 --> 00:17:14,472
No Dad! No! It's me! It's me!

152
00:17:14,472 --> 00:17:17,266
I'll just hang the boy here
in case we change our minds.

153
00:17:20,644 --> 00:17:24,648
Wait... That's our Turtles Run.
That's our eldest.

154
00:17:24,648 --> 00:17:26,150
Yes it's me. It's your eldest!

155
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:31,489
In that case,
a crush for my eldest...

156
00:17:35,075 --> 00:17:37,369
...and a crush for my youngest.

157
00:17:38,662 --> 00:17:40,998
[Mother] Tapir it is.

158
00:17:40,998 --> 00:17:43,334
[Blunted moaning]

159
00:17:43,334 --> 00:17:48,297
[both hollering]

160
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:58,724
[all laughing]

161
00:18:47,064 --> 00:18:49,066
One day, old man!

162
00:18:49,066 --> 00:18:51,402
One day you won't be able
to run anymore!

163
00:19:09,086 --> 00:19:12,256
[man] And a Man sat alone.

164
00:19:13,674 --> 00:19:16,927
Drenched deep in sadness.

165
00:19:16,927 --> 00:19:20,347
And all the animals
drew near to him and said:

166
00:19:20,347 --> 00:19:24,143
"We do not like
to see you so sad...

167
00:19:25,936 --> 00:19:30,441
"Ask us for whatever you wish
and you shall have it."

168
00:19:30,441 --> 00:19:34,778
The Man said:
"I want to have good sight."

169
00:19:36,196 --> 00:19:39,408
The vulture replied:
"You shall have mine."

170
00:19:42,453 --> 00:19:45,623
The Man said:
"I want to be strong."

171
00:19:49,335 --> 00:19:51,128
The jaguar said:

172
00:19:53,464 --> 00:19:56,425
"You shall be strong like me."

173
00:19:58,385 --> 00:20:04,224
Then the Man said: "I long to
know the secrets of the earth."

174
00:20:05,809 --> 00:20:10,814
The serpent replied:
"I will show them to you."

175
00:20:12,691 --> 00:20:15,152
And so it went
with all the animals.

176
00:20:16,904 --> 00:20:19,823
And when the Man had all the
gifts that they could give...

177
00:20:19,823 --> 00:20:21,492
...he left.

178
00:20:23,035 --> 00:20:26,246
Then the owl said
to the other animals:

179
00:20:26,246 --> 00:20:30,125
"Now the Man knows much
and is able to do many things...

180
00:20:31,210 --> 00:20:34,546
"Suddenly I am afraid."

181
00:20:37,758 --> 00:20:40,552
The deer said:
"The Man has all that he needs."

182
00:20:41,679 --> 00:20:44,348
"Now his sadness will stop."

183
00:20:44,348 --> 00:20:46,350
But the owl replied: "No."

184
00:20:49,019 --> 00:20:51,897
"I saw a hole in the Man...

185
00:20:51,897 --> 00:20:56,777
"Deep like a hunger
he will never fill...

186
00:20:56,777 --> 00:21:02,199
"It is what makes him sad
and what makes him want."

187
00:21:05,452 --> 00:21:08,539
"He will go on taking
and taking...

188
00:21:09,707 --> 00:21:13,711
"Until one day the World
will say:

189
00:21:13,711 --> 00:21:17,840
"I am no more and I have
nothing left to give."

190
00:21:24,847 --> 00:21:25,848
[drum beating]

191
00:21:27,391 --> 00:21:30,978
[indistinct chatter]

192
00:22:04,595 --> 00:22:06,430
Come back to me...

193
00:22:10,768 --> 00:22:12,603
Come back to me.

194
00:22:41,507 --> 00:22:43,509
My son is dancing.

195
00:22:45,219 --> 00:22:47,346
Your son is happy.

196
00:23:17,501 --> 00:23:20,170
[dog barking]

197
00:23:25,843 --> 00:23:28,846
[heartbeat]

198
00:23:39,731 --> 00:23:41,441
What do you want?

199
00:23:41,441 --> 00:23:44,444
[panting]

200
00:23:57,416 --> 00:23:59,168
Run!

201
00:24:10,762 --> 00:24:13,223
[moaning]

202
00:24:14,725 --> 00:24:18,729
Now that you're up,
can you please kill that dog?

203
00:24:31,909 --> 00:24:33,952
The dog.

204
00:24:36,038 --> 00:24:38,790
[dog continues barking]

205
00:25:34,596 --> 00:25:36,598
[dog whimpers, stops barking]

206
00:26:01,581 --> 00:26:03,166
Get up! Get up! Now!

207
00:26:11,550 --> 00:26:13,552
[screaming]

208
00:26:33,071 --> 00:26:35,949
- [grunting]
- [yelling]

209
00:26:53,383 --> 00:26:55,927
[indistinct screaming]

210
00:27:05,228 --> 00:27:07,898
[both grunting]

211
00:27:18,909 --> 00:27:20,952
Go to the forest.

212
00:27:20,952 --> 00:27:22,788
Run! Do not look back.

213
00:27:43,683 --> 00:27:46,603
[panting, shouts]

214
00:27:48,605 --> 00:27:50,774
No! No! I am afraid!

215
00:27:50,774 --> 00:27:53,151
Look into my eyes.
Look into my eyes.

216
00:27:53,151 --> 00:27:54,653
Be strong...

217
00:27:54,653 --> 00:27:56,363
I am afraid!

218
00:27:56,363 --> 00:27:57,906
Be strong.

219
00:28:37,571 --> 00:28:40,657
- [crying]
- [shouting]

220
00:28:48,331 --> 00:28:50,959
[baby wails]

221
00:28:56,339 --> 00:28:57,174
Tie him up!

222
00:29:16,568 --> 00:29:18,737
[screams]

223
00:30:15,335 --> 00:30:16,378
Father!

224
00:30:17,754 --> 00:30:19,923
The others. I have to help.

225
00:30:21,091 --> 00:30:23,093
No, don't leave us!

226
00:30:23,093 --> 00:30:26,096
I will come back, I promise.

227
00:30:26,096 --> 00:30:27,597
Don't you leave!

228
00:30:27,597 --> 00:30:28,473
I promise.

229
00:30:28,473 --> 00:30:29,599
Stay, please stay.

230
00:30:29,599 --> 00:30:30,767
Father, don't go.

231
00:30:31,768 --> 00:30:33,311
[shouts in Mayan]

232
00:30:39,693 --> 00:30:42,946
[crying out]

233
00:30:46,741 --> 00:30:49,786
- [bone crunching]
- [screaming]

234
00:30:55,041 --> 00:30:59,337
[both shouting]

235
00:31:04,009 --> 00:31:06,011
- [screaming]
- [chuckling]

236
00:31:27,365 --> 00:31:28,783
Very nice.

237
00:32:15,789 --> 00:32:16,831
Stop!

238
00:32:25,632 --> 00:32:26,925
Tie him up!

239
00:32:31,304 --> 00:32:32,722
I want him alive.

240
00:32:53,243 --> 00:32:54,536
Sorry Father.

241
00:33:13,638 --> 00:33:15,557
That's enough!

242
00:33:26,151 --> 00:33:27,944
Stand him up.

243
00:33:35,660 --> 00:33:37,287
Move away.

244
00:33:51,134 --> 00:33:52,927
My son.

245
00:34:03,813 --> 00:34:05,607
Don't be afraid.

246
00:34:12,655 --> 00:34:13,656
[gasps]

247
00:35:03,915 --> 00:35:06,376
Almost...

248
00:35:12,423 --> 00:35:13,716
[gasps]

249
00:35:21,307 --> 00:35:23,893
...that's your name.

250
00:35:24,894 --> 00:35:28,064
"Almost".

251
00:35:31,317 --> 00:35:34,362
[indistinct wailing]

252
00:35:37,407 --> 00:35:40,410
[indistinct chattering]

253
00:35:43,955 --> 00:35:46,416
Our life is over.

254
00:35:51,838 --> 00:35:53,131
Shame...

255
00:36:01,180 --> 00:36:02,432
Shame!

256
00:36:06,603 --> 00:36:08,646
Cowards!

257
00:36:12,942 --> 00:36:14,777
[both shouting]

258
00:36:36,966 --> 00:36:40,637
[weeping]

259
00:38:36,836 --> 00:38:38,379
[whispers indistinctly]

260
00:39:08,993 --> 00:39:13,039
- [gasps]
- [cries out, sobs]

261
00:39:42,318 --> 00:39:44,112
Let's move!

262
00:40:52,471 --> 00:40:55,391
[children crying]

263
00:41:20,917 --> 00:41:23,085
[babies crying]

264
00:41:57,495 --> 00:41:59,121
[cries out]

265
00:42:01,123 --> 00:42:03,793
[yells out in Mayan]

266
00:42:03,793 --> 00:42:05,544
We move out now.

267
00:42:05,544 --> 00:42:06,963
They are back.

268
00:42:10,007 --> 00:42:11,342
Get up!

269
00:42:14,136 --> 00:42:15,596
Heave!

270
00:42:22,812 --> 00:42:25,523
Cut Rock, you forgot to duck.

271
00:42:28,526 --> 00:42:29,819
Hold still.

272
00:42:39,537 --> 00:42:40,663
Can you see?

273
00:42:43,082 --> 00:42:44,500
Yes.

274
00:42:44,500 --> 00:42:46,294
Get back to your line.

275
00:43:10,568 --> 00:43:14,530
- [panting]
- [indistinct chatter]

276
00:43:21,287 --> 00:43:25,875
[children shout out, cry]

277
00:43:47,730 --> 00:43:48,898
Come with us...

278
00:44:17,468 --> 00:44:21,222
[gasping]

279
00:44:41,283 --> 00:44:42,451
Get up.

280
00:44:55,047 --> 00:44:57,299
Leave him alone, "Almost".

281
00:44:59,468 --> 00:45:01,345
I said get up.

282
00:45:09,854 --> 00:45:11,856
- [grunting]
- [straining]

283
00:45:29,915 --> 00:45:32,168
Up, up...

284
00:45:32,168 --> 00:45:33,711
...that's it.

285
00:45:35,838 --> 00:45:37,173
Let's go!

286
00:45:41,051 --> 00:45:43,971
This man is
a good friend of yours...

287
00:46:02,698 --> 00:46:05,034
[wheezing]

288
00:46:11,582 --> 00:46:14,710
[children wailing]

289
00:46:18,881 --> 00:46:20,841
Don't worry...

290
00:46:24,386 --> 00:46:26,388
I'll take care of them.

291
00:46:29,308 --> 00:46:31,602
They are mine now.

292
00:46:38,901 --> 00:46:42,947
Gentle Ixchel.
Tender mother of mercy.

293
00:46:44,782 --> 00:46:49,912
Keep them from harm.
Please. Keep them.

294
00:47:16,021 --> 00:47:17,731
[groaning]

295
00:47:25,823 --> 00:47:27,449
One more.

296
00:47:51,056 --> 00:47:52,766
Ready?

297
00:48:18,500 --> 00:48:22,004
[indistinct shouting]

298
00:48:29,678 --> 00:48:30,721
[gasps, grunting]

299
00:48:40,689 --> 00:48:42,524
[straining]

300
00:48:53,702 --> 00:48:55,245
Hold on! Hold on!

301
00:48:59,208 --> 00:49:00,751
Wait...

302
00:49:02,294 --> 00:49:04,088
...let's see what happens.

303
00:49:12,096 --> 00:49:13,013
That's it!

304
00:49:20,229 --> 00:49:21,438
Hurry!

305
00:49:22,398 --> 00:49:24,358
Pull! Be strong!

306
00:49:43,419 --> 00:49:45,295
Yes! You did it!

307
00:49:45,295 --> 00:49:47,631
[laughing]

308
00:49:49,091 --> 00:49:50,759
Good work!

309
00:50:03,605 --> 00:50:06,316
Can you breathe?...Good.

310
00:50:11,780 --> 00:50:15,033
[thudding]

311
00:50:36,138 --> 00:50:37,014
[man] Wait here.

312
00:51:10,380 --> 00:51:12,049
What's become of my capture?

313
00:51:15,844 --> 00:51:17,304
Dead weight.

314
00:51:19,014 --> 00:51:21,225
He nearly took
the rest with him.

315
00:51:23,519 --> 00:51:25,187
I let him go.

316
00:51:29,441 --> 00:51:31,193
You. Let him go?

317
00:51:38,242 --> 00:51:41,745
Shall we now do what you want?

318
00:51:46,083 --> 00:51:49,044
Let us try that.

319
00:52:07,855 --> 00:52:09,106
[speaks Mayan]

320
00:52:12,317 --> 00:52:15,112
Don't let any others go.

321
00:52:21,785 --> 00:52:23,579
Let's move.

322
00:52:23,579 --> 00:52:26,999
[man shouts in Mayan]

323
00:52:28,125 --> 00:52:30,627
[Jaguar Paw winces]

324
00:52:38,343 --> 00:52:41,597
Get up "Almost".

325
00:52:41,597 --> 00:52:45,142
We don't want
to lose you just yet.

326
00:52:46,518 --> 00:52:49,813
[woman singing]

327
00:53:24,806 --> 00:53:27,643
[speaking in Mayan]

328
00:53:35,317 --> 00:53:37,319
Stand up, boy.

329
00:53:46,078 --> 00:53:49,331
You proved yourself
today, my son.

330
00:53:49,331 --> 00:53:53,126
You're now worthy to stand
with the rest of us.

331
00:53:55,671 --> 00:53:58,215
Thank you Father.

332
00:54:08,266 --> 00:54:09,643
Take it...

333
00:54:10,394 --> 00:54:11,645
...it's yours.

334
00:54:15,732 --> 00:54:18,360
It has taken many lives.

335
00:54:30,747 --> 00:54:32,207
Get some rest.

336
00:54:46,722 --> 00:54:48,140
Resting brothers...

337
00:54:48,140 --> 00:54:52,561
...fathers, mothers, wives.

338
00:54:52,561 --> 00:54:57,649
You felt the cold
of this day's early morning.

339
00:54:57,649 --> 00:55:01,862
Now you cannot feel
the coldness of its night.

340
00:55:04,573 --> 00:55:06,575
She stopped screaming...

341
00:55:08,744 --> 00:55:12,581
...too long before they returned,
she had stopped screaming.

342
00:55:12,581 --> 00:55:15,250
We saw how she fought them.

343
00:55:16,293 --> 00:55:18,128
But in the final moment?

344
00:55:19,755 --> 00:55:21,631
If she let them...

345
00:55:24,301 --> 00:55:25,802
...the Goddess of the Scaffold

346
00:55:25,802 --> 00:55:28,930
shows no mercy
for the weakness...

347
00:55:30,974 --> 00:55:35,437
Her soul waits for yours
in the shade of the Ceiba Tree.

348
00:55:46,615 --> 00:55:48,325
I need to know.

349
00:55:49,826 --> 00:55:54,623
Before this day's end
I will leave this world.

350
00:55:56,541 --> 00:56:02,005
I will take as many of these
bastard dogs with me as I can.

351
00:56:04,341 --> 00:56:09,137
And I will gladly embrace
the torments of hell...

352
00:56:11,306 --> 00:56:14,768
...if I do not find
my Sky Flower there.

353
00:56:14,768 --> 00:56:16,645
[thundering]

354
00:56:21,733 --> 00:56:23,193
Don't rain.

355
00:56:46,007 --> 00:56:49,886
- [indistinct chatter]
- [tree rumbling]

356
00:56:52,848 --> 00:56:54,850
[men shouting]

357
00:57:06,528 --> 00:57:08,363
I am walking here.

358
00:57:26,715 --> 00:57:28,717
[weeping]

359
00:57:41,146 --> 00:57:43,190
Keep away, she has the sickness.

360
00:58:08,757 --> 00:58:10,425
[man] Get back!

361
00:58:16,973 --> 00:58:19,184
- [grunts]
- [moans]

362
00:59:03,311 --> 00:59:05,480
You fear me?

363
00:59:06,856 --> 00:59:09,484
So you should...

364
00:59:09,484 --> 00:59:13,530
...all you who are vile.

365
00:59:16,574 --> 00:59:20,120
Would you like
to know how you will die?

366
00:59:27,168 --> 00:59:31,006
The sacred time is near...

367
00:59:33,174 --> 00:59:37,345
Beware the blackness of day.

368
00:59:40,515 --> 00:59:45,312
Beware the man
who brings the jaguar.

369
00:59:48,189 --> 00:59:53,945
Behold him reborn
from mud and earth...

370
00:59:53,945 --> 00:59:59,826
For the one he takes you to
will cancel the sky...

371
01:00:00,994 --> 01:00:03,830
...and scratch out the earth.

372
01:00:04,956 --> 01:00:07,250
Scratch you out.

373
01:00:08,543 --> 01:00:11,212
And end your world.

374
01:00:17,802 --> 01:00:20,930
He's with us now.

375
01:00:27,896 --> 01:00:31,274
...day will be like night.

376
01:00:31,274 --> 01:00:35,862
And the man jaguar
will lead you to your end.

377
01:00:40,492 --> 01:00:42,535
[indistinct shouting]

378
01:01:46,808 --> 01:01:49,102
Where are they taking us?

379
01:01:53,398 --> 01:01:57,819
We tell stories
of a place stone-built.

380
01:01:59,320 --> 01:02:00,864
What happens there?

381
01:02:01,823 --> 01:02:03,199
I do not know...

382
01:02:04,742 --> 01:02:08,288
...but the earth bleeds.

383
01:02:11,332 --> 01:02:13,209
We are near.

384
01:02:54,918 --> 01:02:57,128
Salvation!

385
01:02:57,128 --> 01:03:00,215
He has the laughing sickness.

386
01:03:01,216 --> 01:03:03,218
He likes you!

387
01:03:05,803 --> 01:03:07,055
Help me!

388
01:03:15,396 --> 01:03:17,232
Save me.

389
01:03:25,156 --> 01:03:26,741
Die like a man.

390
01:03:26,741 --> 01:03:28,743
[whimpering]

391
01:05:28,029 --> 01:05:31,324
[chanting]

392
01:05:45,713 --> 01:05:48,132
[growling]

393
01:06:07,318 --> 01:06:08,403
Welcome back.

394
01:06:09,570 --> 01:06:11,614
Have you been successful?

395
01:06:11,614 --> 01:06:12,740
Ask my son.

396
01:06:14,659 --> 01:06:16,244
How many captives?

397
01:06:16,244 --> 01:06:17,245
Deal with my son.

398
01:06:19,330 --> 01:06:20,415
A fair price.

399
01:06:21,833 --> 01:06:23,584
As always, trust me.

400
01:06:24,419 --> 01:06:25,086
Good.

401
01:06:26,754 --> 01:06:29,090
[speaking in Mayan]

402
01:06:42,937 --> 01:06:45,648
How much will you give me?

403
01:06:47,942 --> 01:06:50,111
[shouting indistinctly]

404
01:07:19,640 --> 01:07:21,309
[shouting in Mayan]

405
01:07:26,939 --> 01:07:28,941
[all yelling]

406
01:07:47,376 --> 01:07:49,295
Who will buy this woman?

407
01:07:50,379 --> 01:07:51,714
[man] No...she's too old.

408
01:07:53,049 --> 01:07:55,343
She can be useful.

409
01:07:55,343 --> 01:07:57,053
She can cook...clean...

410
01:07:58,596 --> 01:08:00,681
Useless old woman!

411
01:08:04,352 --> 01:08:05,853
No sale.

412
01:08:11,609 --> 01:08:12,985
Go!

413
01:08:14,070 --> 01:08:15,363
Go on.

414
01:08:19,367 --> 01:08:22,036
[chanting continues]

415
01:09:06,455 --> 01:09:09,041
[indistinct chatter]

416
01:09:37,820 --> 01:09:41,115
- [crowd shouting indistinctly]
- [loud drumming]

417
01:10:01,052 --> 01:10:03,429
[chanting, shouting]

418
01:11:26,721 --> 01:11:29,015
[panting, chanting]

419
01:11:59,295 --> 01:12:02,923
[crowd cheers]

420
01:12:48,385 --> 01:12:52,890
[chanting]

421
01:13:00,981 --> 01:13:03,317
[crowd cheers]

422
01:13:16,163 --> 01:13:20,501
These are the days
of our great lament.

423
01:13:20,501 --> 01:13:22,753
[crowd shouting indistinctly]

424
01:13:24,922 --> 01:13:26,841
The land thirsts.

425
01:13:29,260 --> 01:13:33,681
A great plague
infests our crops.

426
01:13:36,517 --> 01:13:40,563
The scourge of sickness
afflicts us at whim.

427
01:13:46,569 --> 01:13:50,197
They say this strife
has made us weak.

428
01:13:52,408 --> 01:13:54,243
That we have become empty.

429
01:13:57,037 --> 01:13:59,331
They say that we rot.

430
01:14:11,051 --> 01:14:13,888
Great people
of the banner of the sun...

431
01:14:14,722 --> 01:14:16,223
I say...

432
01:14:17,391 --> 01:14:19,226
...we are strong.

433
01:14:23,731 --> 01:14:25,774
We are a people of destiny.

434
01:14:30,571 --> 01:14:33,866
Destined to be
the masters of time.

435
01:14:37,912 --> 01:14:41,207
Destined to be
nearest to the gods.

436
01:14:57,139 --> 01:15:00,267
Mighty Kukulkan!

437
01:15:01,936 --> 01:15:06,440
Whose fury could scorch
this earth to oblivion...

438
01:15:09,109 --> 01:15:11,987
Let us appease you
with this sacrifice.

439
01:15:11,987 --> 01:15:14,657
To exalt you in your glory.

440
01:15:14,657 --> 01:15:17,284
To make our people prosper.

441
01:15:18,410 --> 01:15:21,121
To prepare for your return.

442
01:15:24,166 --> 01:15:27,503
Warrior, unafraid and willing!

443
01:15:27,503 --> 01:15:30,381
With your blood
you renew the world!

444
01:15:30,381 --> 01:15:32,174
From age to age.

445
01:15:33,634 --> 01:15:35,302
Thanks be to you.

446
01:15:35,302 --> 01:15:37,554
- [crowd cheers]
- [gasping]

447
01:15:49,984 --> 01:15:52,152
The heart of god!

448
01:16:08,419 --> 01:16:10,504
[chanting]

449
01:17:04,725 --> 01:17:09,063
- [heartbeat pounding]
- [speaking in Mayan]

450
01:17:34,254 --> 01:17:36,548
[gasping]

451
01:18:11,208 --> 01:18:13,460
[inhales sharply]

452
01:18:35,858 --> 01:18:38,152
Come back to me.

453
01:18:47,077 --> 01:18:48,954
Brother...

454
01:18:50,831 --> 01:18:52,666
Journey well...

455
01:18:54,835 --> 01:18:55,711
No.

456
01:18:57,212 --> 01:18:58,338
I can't go.

457
01:18:59,882 --> 01:19:01,467
Not now...

458
01:19:12,769 --> 01:19:15,189
[man speaks indistinctly]

459
01:19:27,159 --> 01:19:28,494
[giggles]

460
01:20:00,484 --> 01:20:04,738
[warbled chanting]

461
01:20:22,923 --> 01:20:26,301
[crowd moaning]

462
01:20:57,124 --> 01:20:59,918
[crowd wailing]

463
01:21:21,189 --> 01:21:26,028
People of the banner
of the sun do not fear.

464
01:21:26,987 --> 01:21:29,489
Rejoice!

465
01:21:29,489 --> 01:21:33,493
Kukulkan has drunk
his fill of blood.

466
01:21:33,493 --> 01:21:36,288
We have sated his thirst.

467
01:21:37,414 --> 01:21:39,082
Great god.

468
01:21:40,083 --> 01:21:42,586
Show us that you are pleased.

469
01:21:42,586 --> 01:21:46,173
Let your light return upon us.

470
01:21:53,055 --> 01:21:55,223
[all cheer]

471
01:22:11,198 --> 01:22:15,869
- [muttering]
- [laughing]

472
01:22:51,571 --> 01:22:53,615
What of these captives?

473
01:22:58,328 --> 01:23:00,247
Dispose of them.

474
01:23:02,499 --> 01:23:04,710
- [shouting indistinctly]
- [men panting]

475
01:23:34,656 --> 01:23:36,825
I need a finisher.

476
01:23:41,872 --> 01:23:43,165
You.

477
01:23:49,296 --> 01:23:50,839
Release them.

478
01:23:59,139 --> 01:24:00,766
You watch.

479
01:24:08,774 --> 01:24:10,233
- [gasps]
- [grunts]

480
01:24:21,661 --> 01:24:22,704
I'm ready!

481
01:24:27,709 --> 01:24:30,670
There's your jungle
beyond the corn.

482
01:24:33,673 --> 01:24:35,050
Go to it.

483
01:24:35,884 --> 01:24:37,302
You're free...

484
01:24:39,179 --> 01:24:40,514
...now run.

485
01:24:43,850 --> 01:24:45,185
I said run.

486
01:24:49,606 --> 01:24:50,857
Run!

487
01:25:22,889 --> 01:25:24,724
- [grunts]
- [men cheer]

488
01:25:27,894 --> 01:25:31,731
[shuddering]

489
01:26:04,514 --> 01:26:05,599
Not bad.

490
01:26:08,768 --> 01:26:10,604
[gasping heavily]

491
01:26:23,783 --> 01:26:25,118
Your turn.

492
01:26:32,959 --> 01:26:34,461
Run.

493
01:26:42,010 --> 01:26:44,137
[panting]

494
01:27:31,226 --> 01:27:33,478
[all cheer]

495
01:27:37,565 --> 01:27:40,902
[straining]

496
01:27:50,370 --> 01:27:51,830
Run!

497
01:28:13,059 --> 01:28:15,478
- [grunts]
- [men laugh]

498
01:28:24,070 --> 01:28:26,406
[men muttering]

499
01:29:06,321 --> 01:29:07,906
Sleep.

500
01:29:08,865 --> 01:29:11,117
Sleep, sleep now my son.

501
01:29:12,202 --> 01:29:14,496
The pain will be no more.

502
01:29:16,456 --> 01:29:17,749
Sleep.

503
01:29:52,826 --> 01:29:55,537
[all hollering]

504
01:30:49,048 --> 01:30:50,675
[panting]

505
01:31:12,071 --> 01:31:15,200
- [shouts]
- [flies buzzing]

506
01:32:57,218 --> 01:33:00,221
[gasping, groaning]

507
01:34:27,600 --> 01:34:31,270
[animal growls]

508
01:34:36,192 --> 01:34:39,946
[animal snarls loudly]

509
01:35:07,807 --> 01:35:09,976
He didn't come this way.

510
01:35:23,239 --> 01:35:25,199
He's in the trees.

511
01:35:26,993 --> 01:35:28,202
Spread out.

512
01:35:29,120 --> 01:35:30,621
Keep your eyes up.

513
01:35:48,931 --> 01:35:50,141
[growling]

514
01:35:53,019 --> 01:35:54,061
Quiet.

515
01:36:00,943 --> 01:36:03,196
[leaves rustling]

516
01:36:05,698 --> 01:36:06,866
He's coming right at us.

517
01:36:18,878 --> 01:36:21,464
[rapid footsteps approaching]

518
01:36:23,591 --> 01:36:24,258
There!

519
01:37:07,301 --> 01:37:10,805
- [snarling]
- [screaming]

520
01:37:29,490 --> 01:37:31,284
[yelling, grunting]

521
01:37:50,636 --> 01:37:53,973
[rumbling]

522
01:38:22,501 --> 01:38:25,212
He would have wanted me
to have it.

523
01:38:27,381 --> 01:38:30,343
The omen is bad...

524
01:38:32,261 --> 01:38:36,599
Mighty Ek Chuah we beg you...

525
01:38:36,599 --> 01:38:40,853
Forgive us for this trespass
against your son the Jaguar.

526
01:38:42,855 --> 01:38:45,358
The omen is bad...

527
01:38:47,068 --> 01:38:49,904
Lift yourself up
Drunkards Four...

528
01:38:49,904 --> 01:38:52,907
...the omen was foretold...

529
01:38:55,284 --> 01:38:59,455
...and now we have
a fear more grave...

530
01:38:59,455 --> 01:39:02,875
...today I saw the day
become like night...

531
01:39:07,838 --> 01:39:09,382
[grunts]

532
01:39:09,382 --> 01:39:13,052
I saw a man run
with the Jaguar...

533
01:39:16,931 --> 01:39:21,018
...we must not let this man
make feet from us.

534
01:39:21,769 --> 01:39:22,937
[man] Enough.

535
01:39:26,732 --> 01:39:28,567
Your words mean nothing.

536
01:39:29,944 --> 01:39:32,154
He runs because he is afraid.

537
01:39:33,572 --> 01:39:37,201
When I catch him,
I will peel his skin...

538
01:39:40,246 --> 01:39:42,957
...and have him
watch me wear it.

539
01:39:50,673 --> 01:39:51,924
We leave now.

540
01:40:30,921 --> 01:40:32,965
[panting, straining]

541
01:40:37,136 --> 01:40:39,889
- [thudding]
- [gasping]

542
01:41:21,847 --> 01:41:24,016
[dog barking]

543
01:41:43,369 --> 01:41:44,703
- [snarling]
- [gasping]

544
01:41:56,924 --> 01:41:59,552
- [thudding]
- [whimpering]

545
01:41:59,552 --> 01:42:00,719
Stay back.

546
01:42:34,628 --> 01:42:37,047
- [squealing]
- [shouting]

547
01:42:56,650 --> 01:42:58,777
- [panting]
- [uneven footsteps running]

548
01:43:11,665 --> 01:43:12,791
Here!

549
01:43:21,842 --> 01:43:24,011
[yelping, moaning]

550
01:43:26,805 --> 01:43:28,974
[wheezing]

551
01:43:37,358 --> 01:43:39,485
The omen was bad...

552
01:43:43,197 --> 01:43:44,323
He's fucked.

553
01:43:47,660 --> 01:43:49,036
Help...please...

554
01:43:49,870 --> 01:43:51,163
Hanging Moss...

555
01:43:52,831 --> 01:43:54,458
See him out.

556
01:44:14,895 --> 01:44:18,565
Open your veins. It's quicker.

557
01:44:31,286 --> 01:44:33,372
Travel well.

558
01:47:05,691 --> 01:47:07,693
[exhaling heavily]

559
01:47:39,224 --> 01:47:41,935
So much for your prophecies.

560
01:47:47,816 --> 01:47:49,067
It's not over!

561
01:47:58,285 --> 01:48:00,537
[gasping]

562
01:48:15,093 --> 01:48:17,429
I am Jaguar Paw...

563
01:48:17,429 --> 01:48:18,972
Son of Flint Sky...

564
01:48:20,432 --> 01:48:23,769
My father hunted
this forest before me...

565
01:48:25,520 --> 01:48:27,481
My name is Jaguar Paw.

566
01:48:28,315 --> 01:48:29,942
I am a hunter.

567
01:48:31,526 --> 01:48:34,947
This is my forest.

568
01:48:34,947 --> 01:48:39,493
And my sons will hunt it with
their sons after I am gone...

569
01:48:42,371 --> 01:48:43,622
Come on!

570
01:48:46,291 --> 01:48:48,543
We are going over.

571
01:48:48,543 --> 01:48:51,296
We climb down around.

572
01:48:52,547 --> 01:48:55,342
We cannot let him get away.

573
01:48:55,342 --> 01:48:56,551
We cannot afford...

574
01:48:56,551 --> 01:48:58,929
[gasping]

575
01:49:16,697 --> 01:49:18,824
We all jump.

576
01:49:23,036 --> 01:49:25,956
[shouting]

577
01:49:43,807 --> 01:49:46,184
[gasps]

578
01:50:37,235 --> 01:50:39,780
- [gulping]
- [mud bubbling]

579
01:51:16,191 --> 01:51:18,235
[inhaling sharply]

580
01:51:49,057 --> 01:51:53,061
[panting]

581
01:52:15,834 --> 01:52:17,502
I am Jaguar Paw.

582
01:52:19,337 --> 01:52:21,173
This is my forest.

583
01:52:23,258 --> 01:52:25,969
And I am not afraid.

584
01:52:41,693 --> 01:52:44,863
[buzzing]

585
01:53:05,550 --> 01:53:07,886
[all screaming]

586
01:54:33,388 --> 01:54:35,974
You go. I'll wait here.

587
01:55:30,111 --> 01:55:34,324
[wheezing]

588
01:56:38,221 --> 01:56:40,724
- [thunder rumbles]
- [gasping]

589
01:57:06,624 --> 01:57:08,793
[straining]

590
01:57:12,380 --> 01:57:14,632
- [gasps]
- [wails]

591
01:57:46,247 --> 01:57:48,666
[wheezing]

592
01:57:53,671 --> 01:57:56,382
- [blows]
- [winces]

593
01:58:15,109 --> 01:58:16,569
[moans, yells]

594
01:58:53,231 --> 01:58:59,237
[both breathing heavily]

595
01:59:50,121 --> 01:59:54,292
[wheezing]

596
02:00:05,470 --> 02:00:07,305
Almost...

597
02:00:20,985 --> 02:00:24,572
[thundering]

598
02:00:34,165 --> 02:00:36,834
Resting fathers,
fly me your strength.

599
02:00:44,842 --> 02:00:45,843
[growls]

600
02:00:56,521 --> 02:01:02,360
- [shivering]
- [crying]

601
02:01:03,861 --> 02:01:05,655
Get up here.

602
02:01:10,618 --> 02:01:13,955
- [gasps, grunting]
- [yelling]

603
02:01:20,545 --> 02:01:22,088
Go back!

604
02:01:49,407 --> 02:01:51,492
- [gasping]
- [speaks Mayan]

605
02:01:51,492 --> 02:01:52,785
Quick!

606
02:01:52,785 --> 02:01:53,745
Hurry up!

607
02:01:54,579 --> 02:01:55,913
[arrow whizzing]

608
02:02:09,010 --> 02:02:10,762
[straining]

609
02:02:41,167 --> 02:02:43,169
[gasps]

610
02:03:59,370 --> 02:04:01,956
[exhales]

611
02:05:12,235 --> 02:05:16,072
[pushing]

612
02:05:43,849 --> 02:05:48,062
- [crying]
- [gulping]

613
02:07:39,298 --> 02:07:42,676
[baby wailing]

614
02:08:20,631 --> 02:08:22,466
What are they?

615
02:08:24,135 --> 02:08:25,970
They bring men.

616
02:08:30,641 --> 02:08:32,518
Should we go to them?

617
02:08:40,818 --> 02:08:42,653
We should go to the forest.

618
02:08:49,535 --> 02:08:51,454
To seek a new beginning.

619
02:08:56,584 --> 02:08:58,002
Come Turtles Run...

